This MATLAB software implements a mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with global and local boostings for estimating
the complex time-varying regression models.

How to run the mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with global and local boosting steps.

The data we use for this example is given in Zdata.mat (simulated data) and FamaFrenchData.mat (Real Data).


The matlab code for global boosting steps:

1) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Global_Rep_MeanField_RealData.m: run a mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with global boosting steps. Reparameterisation trick is used to update 
the precision matrix for each component. 

2) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Global_Rep_MeanField.m: run a mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with global boosting steps. The control variate method is used to update the precision
matrix for each component.

3) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Global_Rep_RealData.m: run a mixture of Gaussians variational approximation with local boosting steps.

4) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Global.m: 

5) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Local_Rep_MeanField.m

6) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Local_Rep_RealData.m

7) VB_StateSpaceRegression_Local_Rep.m:

obtain_index_full_randomeffect.m

-- to obtain the index of the random effects in the precision matrix

obtain_grad_logposterior_logit_some.m

-- main file used to obtain the derivative of the log-posterior of the random effects logistic model with respect to the model parameters and random effects.

obtain_grad_q.m

-- Main file used to obtain the derivative of the log of the mixture of gaussians density with respect to model parameters and random effects.

initialisation_global_update_used.m

-- obtaining the initial values of the variational means and diagonal components of the precision matrix of the random effects (Global Boosting).

initialisation_local_update_used.m

-- obtaining the initial values of the variational means and diagonal components of the precision matrix of the random effects (Local Boosting).

initialisation_global_parameter.m

-- obtaining the initial values of the variational means of the global parameters.

SampleFromMixture_Weight.m

-- generate samples of random effects and parameters from the mixture of Gaussians variational approximation.


Calculating_RKL_higherdim.m

-- function to calculate the criteria to select poorly approximate random effects.


Other useful functions are provided in the folder.

The user need to add the path to the results folder to generate the figures in section 6.1.